<title>GERMANY: Germany lowers yields on some treasury notes.</title>
<headline>Germany lowers yields on some treasury notes.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German government has lowered the nominal interest rates and yields on its treasury notes due January 1, 2003 and January 2004, the Bundesbank said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The yield on the six-year note &quot;type A&quot; has been dropped to 4.85 percent from 5.13 percent while the seven-year note &quot;type B&quot; remains at 5.24 percent.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
